WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.667 --> 00:00:21.097
Tina: Okay, Danny, I’ll push you over to Brad.

2
00:00:21.098 --> 00:00:29.575
Tina: Hmm. I hope this doesn’t hurt him! Here goes!

3
00:00:29.576 --> 00:00:31.970
Tina: There we go! It’s working!

4
00:00:31.971 --> 00:00:33.965
Danny: Good thinking, Tina!

5
00:00:33.966 --> 00:00:36.439
Tina: Now let’s get Brad unfrozen.

6
00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:40.494
Danny: Great!

7
00:00:40.495 --> 00:00:42.875
Tina: Brad, are you okay?

8
00:00:42.876 --> 00:00:44.879
Brad: I think so.

9
00:00:44.880 --> 00:00:46.874
Danny: How did this happen?

10
00:00:46.875 --> 00:00:50.731
Brad: I think we stood still for too long.

11
00:00:50.732 --> 00:00:53.348
Tina: I told you to keep moving!

12
00:00:53.349 --> 00:00:55.964
Brad: Yes, but you’re always saying that!

13
00:00:55.965 --> 00:01:04.546
Tina: Start doing jumping jacks right now!

14
00:01:04.547 --> 00:01:07.139
Danny: We can’t do this forever.

15
00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:12.084
Danny: I’m bored. Let’s practice taekwondo instead!

16
00:01:12.085 --> 00:01:14.818
Brad: I don’t know how to do taekwondo.

17
00:01:14.819 --> 00:01:17.841
Danny: Use your imagination. Pretend!

18
00:01:17.842 --> 00:01:22.495
Brad: You mean like this?

19
00:01:22.496 --> 00:01:26.262
Brad: I’m tired. Can’t we try to use our minds?

20
00:01:26.263 --> 00:01:29.773
Brad: That would be better than jumping around.

21
00:01:29.774 --> 00:01:31.944
Danny: There’s still the clay.

22
00:01:31.945 --> 00:01:37.871
Tina: What could you make to keep us warm?

23
00:01:37.872 --> 00:01:40.442
Brad: A house?

24
00:01:40.443 --> 00:01:43.950
Danny: There’s not enough clay for that!

25
00:01:43.951 --> 00:01:46.227
Tina: Jackets and mittens?

26
00:01:46.228 --> 00:01:49.234
Danny: There’s not enough for that either.

27
00:01:49.235 --> 00:01:52.156
Think of something smaller.

28
00:01:52.157 --> 00:01:54.204
Tina: Like what?

29
00:01:54.205 --> 00:01:56.897
Brad: What is warm and small?

30
00:01:56.898 --> 00:01:59.145
Tina: One mitten?

31
00:01:59.146 --> 00:02:03.488
Danny: That won’t keep us all warm.

32
00:02:03.489 --> 00:02:05.356
Tina: What then?

33
00:02:05.357 --> 00:02:07.966
Danny: What about a big fire?

34
00:02:07.967 --> 00:02:10.504
Brad: That’s a great idea!

35
00:02:10.505 --> 00:02:13.823
Tina: A fire to melt all this snow!

36
00:02:13.824 --> 00:02:15.410
Brad: I don’t know.

37
00:02:15.411 --> 00:02:17.638
A fire can be very dangerous.

38
00:02:17.639 --> 00:02:20.193
Brad: What if it gets out of control?

39
00:02:20.194 --> 00:02:24.134
Danny: You’re right. It’s too dangerous.

40
00:02:24.135 --> 00:02:27.237
Tina: What about something smaller?

41
00:02:27.238 --> 00:02:29.422
Danny: Wait! I’ve got it!

42
00:02:29.423 --> 00:02:32.257
I know what will work!

43
00:02:32.258 --> 00:02:34.856
Tina: I hope it’s something good!

44
00:02:34.857 --> 00:02:37.101
Brad: What is it, Danny?

45
00:02:37.102 --> 00:02:39.922
Danny: Just a little more . . .

46
00:02:39.923 --> 00:02:43.686
Tina: Hurry, Danny. You don’t want to freeze again.

47
00:02:43.687 --> 00:02:46.857
Brad: We’re all freezing again!

48
00:02:46.858 --> 00:02:49.390
Danny: I’ve almost got it.

49
00:02:49.391 --> 00:02:51.012
Brad & Tina: Hurry!

50
00:02:51.013 --> 00:02:58.167
Danny: Just one more minute. There!
